Z closes 6 of 13 OPEN cells. Worst SSIM2 -0.18 (within 0.3 budget). All bytes
byte-identical to W44-94's variant Z column (verified row-by-row).

### Variant W (dct32x32=1.27) on narrow cells

W closes 5 cells (1420710 e6 d=5/d=6, 1420710 e8/e9 d=5, 1531677 e8 d=5).
Worst SSIM2 drop -0.17.

### W93_REGR cells (both Z and W)

All 6 cells (1189261 e5/e6 d=6, 1418519 e5/e6 d=5/d=6) byte-identical to
W44-94's "default" column. The W44-29 gate doesn't fire for these images
(mask ≥ 50: 1189261=69.08, 1418519=92.33), so the constant change has no
effect on either side.

The reproducer's "BYTES DIFFER" status on these rows is a measurement
artifact of the bench's baseline path (which forces `hint=Some(false)` +
internal_params override). The shipped path uses the natural production
gate which doesn't fire for these images, so shipped bytes match the
production-default W44-94 numbers EXACTLY (verified — see `w44_95_ship_variant_z_repro_2026-05-19.tsv`).

## Results — wider 3-photo baseline-diff (FAIL)

Both Z and W (and intermediate dct32=1.30) regressed cells outside the
W44-94 cell list. Critical findings:

### Variant Z (dct32x32=1.20) on wider population

| Image | e | d | old_pct | new_pct | bytes_Δ | ssim2_Δ | status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2389166 | 5 | 3 | +2.27% | -0.23% | -574 | **-0.46** | stable |
| 2389166 | 5 | 4 | -0.63% | -0.48% | +26 | **-0.37** | stable |
| 2389166 | 5 | 5 | -0.17% | +0.48% | +98 | -0.10 | stable |
| 2389166 | 6 | 4 | +1.23% | +0.39% | -159 | **-0.82** | stable |
| 2389166 | 7 | 5 | -1.31% | +3.59% | +780 | -0.06 | **FIXED→OPEN** |
| 3637739 | 5 | 5 | +2.27% | +3.10% | +113 | -0.02 | **FIXED→OPEN** |
| 3637739 | 7 | 4 | +2.98% | +4.64% | +270 | -0.03 | **FIXED→OPEN** |

3 FIXED→OPEN flips, worst SSIM2 -0.82 (well outside the 0.3 budget).

### Variant W (dct32x32=1.27) on wider population

| Image | e | d | old_pct | new_pct | bytes_Δ | ssim2_Δ | status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2389166 | 5 | 3 | +2.27% | -1.26% | -811 | **-0.43** | stable |
| 2389166 | 5 | 4 | -0.63% | +1.58% | +397 | **-0.39** | stable |
| 2389166 | 6 | 4 | +1.23% | +2.09% | +162 | **-0.35** | stable |
| 3637739 | 5 | 5 | +2.27% | +3.10% | +113 | -0.02 | **FIXED→OPEN** |
| 3637739 | 7 | 4 | +2.98% | +4.64% | +270 | -0.03 | **FIXED→OPEN** |

2 FIXED→OPEN flips, worst SSIM2 -0.43 (outside 0.3 budget). The 2389166
cells produce paired byte+SSIM2 regressions (e5 d=4: +397 bytes AND -0.39
SSIM2 — strictly worse, not a Pareto trade).

### Intermediate variant dct32x32=1.30 on wider population

| Image | e | d | old_pct | new_pct | bytes_Δ | ssim2_Δ | status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2389166 | 5 | 3 | +2.27% | -0.48% | -633 | **-0.42** | stable |
| 3637739 | 5 | 5 | +2.27% | +3.10% | +113 | -0.02 | **FIXED→OPEN** |
| 3637739 | 7 | 4 | +2.98% | +4.64% | +270 | -0.03 | **FIXED→OPEN** |

Still 2 FIXED→OPEN flips and -0.42 SSIM2 on 2389166. Marginally better
than W but still fails the gate.

## Honest-stop decision

Per W44-95 decision tree:
> If neither [Z nor W]: honest-stop documenting what changed since
> W44-94's measurement.

Both Z and W fail the SSIM2 ≤ 0.3 gate AND have FIXED→OPEN flips on the
wider mask<50 photo population (2389166, 3637739). The W44-94
measurement's narrow 19-cell coverage missed these regressions —
2389166 and 3637739 are also in the W44-29-firing region but exhibit
different RD behavior than 1420710 / 1531677.

W44-94's RC2 honest-stop comment ("1420710 and 1531677 want OPPOSITE
adjustments at d=5") was correct in concept but understated the scope:
2389166 (mask=46.24) and 3637739 (mask=47.80) ALSO want different
adjustments than 1420710 (mask=39.55) and 1531677 (mask=35.63).
A single global constant change cannot satisfy all four.

**Code reverted to W44-29 baseline (dct32=1.34)**. Net OPEN count
unchanged at 13.

## What W44-96 needs

A per-image zenanalyze discriminator (W44-91 pattern) within mask < 50.
Hypothesis: 1420710 / 1531677 (where Z wins) differ from 2389166 / 3637739
(where Z regresses) on at least one of:
- m3_colourfulness
- flat_color_block_ratio
- high_freq_energy_ratio
- edge_density

A W44-96 chunk should:
1. Compute zenanalyze proxies on all 4 photos via `zenanalyze` CLI
2. Find a clean splitter that puts {1420710, 1531677} on one side and
   {2389166, 3637739} on the other
3. Wire the splitter as a sub-gate within `w44_29_lower` (after mask < 50
   confirms photo class, the new gate routes to dct32=1.20/1.27 only on
   the "1420710-class" sub-population)
4. Re-measure all 4 photos to confirm no regressions

